(In the making of the mind\054 the many Babylonian captivity experiences speak\054 across) Tj
T*
(their different times\054 old and new\073 to the old experience the Children of Israel were) Tj
T*
(subjected\054 and to the new\054 scattered peoples today in Asia and Africa\041 The making of) Tj
T*
(the mind in exile does not resemble its making in the homeland\054 so exiles share to a) Tj
T*
(certain degree similar traits in mental structure that differ from those who lived the) Tj
T*
(experience of the homeland\056 Hence the size of the difference in vision and in looking) Tj
T*
(at matters among those exiled for political reasons\054 such as the Palestinians\054) Tj
T*
(Syrians\054 Iraqis\054 Arakanese\054 Turkestanis\054 Somalis and other peoples who faced the) Tj
T*
(existential challenge\054 the extent to which exile made their minds makes a match) Tj
T*
(between their mental structure and those who did not live the same experience) Tj
T*
(almost nonexistent\041) Tj
